cachy-asahi doctor 0.2.0
Original MIT implementation by cachy-asahi contributors, 2026.

Device-tree board identifiers and diagnostic scope follow this project's
scripts/hardware/capture-baseline.py, protected Asahi policy declarations and
M6 tools-functionality inventory. This standalone command does not import the
broader capture/acquisition tools. No CachyOS/chwd/kdump implementation is reused.

This is an observation tool, not hardware validation, production-trust approval
or an automatic repair/installation system. See README.md for collection limits.

Doctor2 default-output volume/mute observations and private Unix-IPC controls
are original 2026 project code under the same MIT license. No WirePlumber or
PipeWire source is copied; optional wpctl is invoked as an installed client.
